+# Research consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14 using live network fetches.
+
+Inventory coverage for the research was: VMware vCenter Server 8.0.2.00300,
+VMware ESXi 8.0 U2c, VMware vSAN 8.0 U2, VMware NSX 4.2.2.1, VMware
+vSphere Replication 8.7.0.4, and VMware Live Site Recovery 9.0.2.2.
+The sources below supplied compatibility, interoperability, sizing, and
+upgrade-path facts for those components and their VCF targets.
+
+- **Upgrade sequence and related issues for VCF 9.1** —
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html
+  — used for the VCF Installer converge/convert/import route when an existing
+  vSphere estate also has NSX, rather than independently upgrading components.
+- **Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products** —
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html
+  — used for the core order NSX, vCenter, ESXi, then storage finalization, and
+  for positioning replication/recovery products ahead of the core upgrades.
+- **Steps to Converge to VMware Live Recovery Appliance 9.0.4 (or newer)** —
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/408127/steps-to-converge-to-vmware-live-recover.html
+  — used for the unsupported direct vSphere Replication 8.7-to-9.x path, the
+  required 8.8 hop, the 9.0.2.2 staging floor, and final 9.0.4 convergence.
+- **vCenter upgrade precheck from version 8.x to 9.x failing due to NSX
+  version** —
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/425164/vcenter-upgrade-precheck-from-version-8x.html
+  — used for importing the standalone NSX 4.x environment into VCF as a
+  workload domain before its managed upgrade and before vCenter 9.x.
+- **NSX Reference Design Guide 4.2** —
+  https://community.broadcom.com/applications-networking-security/viewdocument/nsx-reference-design-guide-42-v10?CommunityKey=b76535ef-c5a2-474d-8270-3e83685f020e&tab=librarydocuments
+  — used for the Large Edge VM selection above the Medium form factor's
+  sub-2-Gbps guideline, multi-uplink load balancing, and the diverse-uplink
+  layout. The fixture's exact 5-Gbps sizing envelope remains pinned locally.
+
+The live publications are mutable and expose more recent maintenance builds
+than this exercise. The architecture intentionally retains the fixture's pinned
+9.1.0.0/9.0.4 targets because the protected snapshot is the reproducible
+implementation authority.
